// The vote shop. One item at launch, which is the whole of what was asked for: Explorer's ring 4
// carries the farm teleport (skill_farming/scripts/farm_teleport.rs2) and had no source at all,
// because the achievement diary that should hand it out is not implemented.
//
// allstock=no matters even with one line of stock: with allstock=yes the shop would BUY any
// tradeable item, and at a shop paid in vote points that would be a point faucet. ~can_sell_obj
// refuses everything at a points shop as well, so this is the second of two locks.
[vote_shop]
scope=shared
size=1
restock=yes
stackall=no
allstock=no
// One ring, always in stock. The price is the obj's own cost= (^vote_price_explorers_ring, 50)
// against shop_sell_multiplier 1000 per mille on the clerk.
//
// THE THIRD NUMBER IS THE RESTOCK RATE IN TICKS, AND IT MUST NOT BE 0. World.processCleanup tops a
// slot up with `item.count < stockcount && tick % stockrate == 0`, and a rate of 0 makes that
// modulo NaN, which is never 0 - the slot would sit at count 0 for the lifetime of the world and
// the first buyer would take the only ring there will ever be. 1 refills on the next tick, which
// for a fixed-price untradeable reward is exactly right: nothing here wants throttling, and 220 of
// this build's shop lines already use 1.
//
// That was only half of why this shop went permanently empty, and the other half was in the engine
// - restocking a NON-STACKABLE item could not write its own count-0 slot. See the comment on that
// branch in engine/src/engine/World.ts.
stock1=explorers_ring_4,1,1
